    "message": "Wait for background jobs to finish instead of polling a short deadline\n\nwait_for_job, the live recompute and frozen-Scenario tests polled a\nDemoJobManager job for 5 or 10 seconds, and the report-before-completed\ntest polled a ProjectAPI run for about 60, so a busy machine could fail\nthem (#143). Both managers run one job at a time, so the tests now queue\na no-op on the worker and wait for it, then check the status. The\ndemo-job handshake events keep their waits but with a 120-second guard\nthat only ends a hung test. With every chunk slowed to take 15 seconds,\nthe old wait_for_job failed at its deadline and the new one passes.\ndocs/testing.md states the rule for new tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
